+## PyJHora Compatibility Exceptions (PyJHora @ 48e57d29b47a3143519910a24866758116467485; source-level only — PyJHora NOT executed)
+1. **Mercury in Virgo:** DSSME Exalted (spec, reference JSON) vs PyJHora `house_strengths_of_planets` Owner.
+2. **Natural-only vs PyJHora sign matrix:** 3 of 84 cells differ — Sun/Cancer (DSSME Friend, PyJHora Neutral), Mercury/Virgo (above), Venus/Sagittarius (DSSME Neutral, PyJHora Friend). Asserted exactly in `dignityBlock.test.ts`.
+3. **Natural friendship tables:** identical to PyJHora `_friendly/_neutral/_enemy_planets` (7×7, 0 mismatches) — MATCH.
+4. **Great Friend / Great Enemy:** exist only in PyJHora's compound tables; never emitted by DSSME (S-01). v1.6 open item #4 records the same gap for DRF.
+5. **Combustion:** PyJHora's two consumers index the lists differently (`charts.py [p-2]` vs `rashmi.py [p_id-1]`) and the lists disagree with each other; DSSME thresholds govern.
+6. **D-9:** DSSME uses the same Traditional-Parasara element-seed rule as `charts.navamsa_chart`, but `floor((deg*9)/30)` is exact at rational boundaries (10° → 4th navamsa) where PyJHora's float floor-division can fall one navamsa short.
+7. **Retrograde (Level 1):** DSSME matches `drik.planets_in_retrograde` (Swiss speed); `charts.planets_in_retrograde` is an elongation-window approximation and is not used.
+
+## S-09 — Pushkara Navamsha (decision NOT taken; NAVAMSHA block not built)
